KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp26
^\[make\.postcondition\.1\] line \d+ postcondition r\.v == x: SUCCESS$
^\[named\.postcondition\.1\] line \d+ postcondition r\.v == x \+ 1: SUCCESS$
^\[fixed\.postcondition\.1\] line \d+ postcondition r\.v == x: SUCCESS$
^\[ref\.postcondition\.1\] line \d+ postcondition .*: SUCCESS$
^\[cref\.postcondition\.1\] line \d+ postcondition .*: SUCCESS$
^\[rref\.postcondition\.1\] line \d+ postcondition .*: SUCCESS$
^\[after_locals\.postcondition\.1\] line \d+ postcondition .*: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ prvalue: one construction: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ named: no extra copy: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ non-copyable: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.7\] line \d+ write through returned reference: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.8\] line \d+ const reference binds: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.12\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
are not checked
--
The postconditions of functions returning a class or a reference were not
checked (a warning): the check held the result in a variable, which would
have copied a class result and copied, not bound, a reference result.  They
are now checked by goto-programs' instrument_cpp_postconditions on the
result object.  thrower's postcondition holds vacuously: it is not checked
when the function throws.  Checked with GCC 16 -fcontracts.
